{%- doc -%}
  Lighthouse Lane custom layer.

  Rendered from layout/theme.liquid immediately after `color-palette`, so
  `ll-custom.css` overrides both token snippets and still loses to app CSS in
  `content_for_header`. This is the theme's only Lighthouse Lane stylesheet
  hook — keep it to one file so the brand layer stays a single request.

  Bevan (wordmark, headings) and Karla (body, nav) render above the fold on
  every template, so their latin subsets are preloaded. Caveat is only ever a
  short aside and is left to load with the stylesheet.

  @example
  {%- render 'll-stylesheets' -%}
{%- enddoc -%}

{{ 'll-bevan-400-latin.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2' }}
{{ 'll-karla-400-800-latin.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2' }}

